-- title:
--   Gauss reductions on X₁(Mp) give exactly the Igusa function field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M$ with $5 \le M$, $M \neq 0$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ given by [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) $\subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ of $X_1(Mp)$ under the coefficientwise embedding [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$; write $\kappa = A/\mathfrak{m}_A$ for the residue field. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is `coeffEmb L` applied to $j_q = q^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{num}}$, assumed nonzero. Finally let $w$ be an `IntegralWeightOneForm` over $\kappa$ of level $M$: a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral power series realising its $q$-expansion, whose reduction `intSeriesC κ w.series` in $\kappa((q))$ is nonzero. Call $(x,y) \in A[[q]]^2$ a Gauss presentation of $f \in K$ if the reduction of $y$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A$ is nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ holds in $L((q))$ after pushing $x, y$ forward along $A \to L$, and let $\bar{x}/\bar{y} \in \kappa((q))$ be the associated reduction. The assertion is twofold: first, every such reduction lies in [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C κ M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35), the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by `x1FunctionFieldC κ M` together with $(\,$`intSeriesC κ w.series`$)^{-1}$; second, every element $z$ of that subfield is of the form $\bar{x}/\bar{y}$ for some $f \in K$ and some Gauss presentation $(x,y)$ of $f$.
--
--   This identifies, modulo the maximal ideal above $p$, the field of reductions of $q$-expansions of functions on $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ with the function field of the Igusa curve $\mathrm{Ig}(M;p)$, obtained from the function field of $X_1(M)$ over $\kappa$ by adjoining the inverse of the reduced weight-one $q$-expansion (a Hasse-invariant root). It is used in the construction and analysis of the integral two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ near the cusp $\infty$, in particular by the statements producing the pair of valuation subrings of $K$ and comparing their residue fields.
